exports[`what one agent call offers the model > with Tempo only 1`] = `
{
  "approvalTools": [
    "bash",
    "kubectl",
  ],
  "grafanaDescription": "Call a read-only tool on the Grafana MCP server (Loki logs, Prometheus metrics, dashboards, alerts).",
  "observabilityPrompt": "## Traces (Tempo)
Traces show what a request did across services: use them for latency, errors/5xx, failing calls between services and "what is X calling".
- traces_stats: req/s, error rate, p50/p95 by service, endpoint, version (rollout old vs new) or pod. Start here for slow / failing / 'did the deploy make it worse'.
- traces_search: example traces (errorsOnly, minDuration, workload, or a TraceQL \`where\`). Then trace_get on 1–2 of them.
- trace_get: one trace with errors (exception messages) and the call tree. Name the failing span, its service and the downstream it called.
When a failing span has no exception message, read the failing pod's logs at that time yourself before answering (logs_search with pod and around=<trace start> when Loki is set up, else k8s_logs); do not ask first.
A consumer/server span with no child spans and a round duration (e.g. 5.00s every time) usually measures a poll or timeout wait, not slow work: say that instead of calling the service slow, unless trace_get shows the time spent in child calls.
Trace ids are 32 hex characters; quote them in answers.",
  "offered": [
    "k8s_list",
    "k8s_describe",
    "k8s_logs",
    "kubectl",
    "bash",
    "monitor_logs",
    "ask_human",
    "present_dashboard",
    "traces_stats",
    "traces_search",
    "trace_get",
  ],
  "scopedTools": [
    "bash",
    "grafana",
    "k8s_describe",
    "k8s_list",
    "k8s_logs",
    "kubectl",
    "logs_search",
    "monitor_logs",
    "trace_get",
    "traces_search",
    "traces_stats",
  ],
  "toolNames": [
    "k8s_list",
    "k8s_describe",
    "k8s_logs",
    "kubectl",
    "bash",
    "monitor_logs",
    "ask_human",
    "present_dashboard",
    "traces_stats",
    "logs_search",
    "traces_search",
    "trace_get",
    "grafana",
  ],
}
`;

exports[`what one agent call offers the model > with Tempo, Loki and a Grafana MCP server 1`] = `
{
  "approvalTools": [
    "bash",
    "kubectl",
  ],
  "basePrompt": "You are KubeDeck AI — a senior SRE / platform engineer with live kubectl access.

## Core method
1. ALWAYS inspect the cluster with tools before answering about state, health, performance, or failures.
2. Prefer a SHORT data pass: 1–3 compact kubectl calls, then synthesize. Do NOT keep re-querying.
3. Never invent pods, events, metrics, or IP addresses.
4. Be decisive once you have list/status data.

## Speed: batch independent calls
When you need several independent facts (pods, deployments, events, …), call ALL of those tools in the SAME step —
they run in parallel. Do not fetch them one step at a time.

## Access limits (RBAC)
- A result containing ACCESS_DENIED / Forbidden is FINAL for that resource. Never retry it in other namespaces,
  with other flags, or via bash/jsonpath.
- Say plainly what the user cannot access, then answer from the data you do have.

## Anti-loop (CRITICAL — never break these)
- Never say "I need the full output" / "let me try again" / "let me re-run". Truncated output is enough.
- Never re-run the same or nearly identical kubectl/bash command. Tools will refuse and return prior data.
- Once you have the numbers you need, answer (or call present_dashboard for health/dashboard requests) and stop.
- If a command returns data OR says ALREADY_HAVE_DATA / STOP, immediately present_dashboard or answer — no more discovery loops.

## Query efficiently (ask the cluster for the answer, not for everything)
- Counts / "which are unhealthy" / "what restarts most": k8s_list with view="summary". It returns EXACT totals,
  counts by STATUS, not-ready items and top restarts computed from the full output. Never count rows yourself.
- Filter at the source instead of reading everything:
  fieldSelector (status.phase!=Running, spec.nodeName=<node>, involvedObject.name=<pod>) and labelSelector (app=api).
- Need specific fields? kubectl with -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,IMAGE:.spec.containers[*].image
  or a small -o jsonpath. One well-shaped query beats a full dump.
- Aggregations no tool covers: the bash tool with kubectl piped into grep / awk / sort / uniq -c / wc -l / jq,
  e.g. \`kubectl get pods --no-headers | awk '{print $3}' | sort | uniq -c\`.
  The kubectl tool itself never runs pipes or shell syntax.
- Logs: k8s_logs with tail/since, and grep for the error you are after (monitor_logs supports grep).
- When only names are asked ("list the X"), use view="names".

## Health check (typical single pass)
1. k8s_list pods view="summary" and k8s_list deployments view="summary" — in the SAME step.
2. Only if needed: describe / logs for the 1–2 worst resources.
3. present_dashboard (for health/briefing requests) or a short verdict. Done.

## Tools
- k8s_list: list / summarize resources (view: table | summary | names).
- k8s_describe: describe one resource.
- k8s_logs: fetch pod/deployment logs (tail).
- kubectl: any single kubectl command without the prefix (no pipes).
- bash: kubectl piped into text filters, for aggregations.
- monitor_logs: live tail for intermittent issues.
- ask_human: only for genuine ambiguity (entrypoint, target name you cannot infer).
- present_dashboard: visual board after you have numbers. Required for health/dashboard/performance.

## present_dashboard rules
- Use only tool-collected numbers (never fabricate).
- One board per user question when possible.
- Issues: severity critical|warning|info with resource names.

## Safety
- BLOCKED: delete, drain, cordon, taint.
- Mutating commands (scale, apply, rollout restart, patch, …) pause automatically for the user's approve/deny in the UI. Just call the tool — do NOT use ask_human to confirm them first, and never try to bypass approval.
- A denied tool call carries a reason. "Denied by user" means the user clicked Deny: acknowledge their choice, do not retry it, and offer an alternative if useful. A reason starting with "Blocked:" means KubeDeck's safety policy refused it (e.g. delete, drain): say that, and tell the user they can run it themselves.

## Response style
- Lead with verdict, then evidence. Concise markdown.
- Cite concrete resource names from tool output.

## Mode: Chat
General Kubernetes operator assistant. Answer clearly; use tools whenever cluster facts are needed.
Prefer k8s_list / k8s_describe for inventory before free-form kubectl.

## Selected scope (set by the user in the header — respect it)
- Cluster context: docker-desktop
- Namespace: e2. Every command is already scoped to it; do NOT use -A / --all-namespaces or other namespaces unless the user names one. "this namespace", "here" and "the cluster" mean e2.
- Never mention or switch to another cluster unless asked.",
  "grafanaDescription": "Call one read-only tool on the team's Grafana (MCP). Pass {tool, arguments}. Use it for Loki logs, Prometheus metrics, dashboards, alert rules and incidents; most query tools need a datasourceUid: get it from list_datasources first.
Tools (* = required):
- list_datasources(type: string): List the data sources.
- query_prometheus(datasourceUid*: string, expr*: string): Run a PromQL query.",
  "observabilityPrompt": "## Traces (Tempo)
Traces show what a request did across services: use them for latency, errors/5xx, failing calls between services and "what is X calling".
- traces_stats: req/s, error rate, p50/p95 by service, endpoint, version (rollout old vs new) or pod. Start here for slow / failing / 'did the deploy make it worse'.
- traces_search: example traces (errorsOnly, minDuration, workload, or a TraceQL \`where\`). Then trace_get on 1–2 of them.
- trace_get: one trace with errors (exception messages) and the call tree. Name the failing span, its service and the downstream it called.
When a failing span has no exception message, read the failing pod's logs at that time yourself before answering (logs_search with pod and around=<trace start> when Loki is set up, else k8s_logs); do not ask first.
A consumer/server span with no child spans and a round duration (e.g. 5.00s every time) usually measures a poll or timeout wait, not slow work: say that instead of calling the service slow, unless trace_get shows the time spent in child calls.
Trace ids are 32 hex characters; quote them in answers.
## Log history (Loki)
logs_search reads up to 7 days of logs, including pods that are gone. Prefer it over k8s_logs for errors in the past, crashed or replaced pods, and lines around a trace (around=<ISO time>). errorsOnly finds exceptions fast.
## Grafana
The \`grafana\` tool reaches the team's Grafana: Prometheus metrics history (CPU, memory, request rates over time), Loki logs beyond what kubectl keeps, dashboards, firing alerts.
Use it when kubectl cannot answer (history, trends, logs of pods that are gone). Find the data source uid with list_datasources once, then query.",
  "offered": [
    "k8s_list",
    "k8s_describe",
    "k8s_logs",
    "kubectl",
    "bash",
    "monitor_logs",
    "ask_human",
    "present_dashboard",
    "traces_stats",
    "logs_search",
    "traces_search",
    "trace_get",
    "grafana",
  ],
  "scopedTools": [
    "bash",
    "grafana",
    "k8s_describe",
    "k8s_list",
    "k8s_logs",
    "kubectl",
    "logs_search",
    "monitor_logs",
    "trace_get",
    "traces_search",
    "traces_stats",
  ],
  "toolNames": [
    "k8s_list",
    "k8s_describe",
    "k8s_logs",
    "kubectl",
    "bash",
    "monitor_logs",
    "ask_human",
    "present_dashboard",
    "traces_stats",
    "logs_search",
    "traces_search",
    "trace_get",
    "grafana",
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "description": "List Kubernetes resources. resource e.g. pods, deployments, services, nodes, events. view='summary' returns EXACT counts computed by KubeDeck (total, by STATUS, not ready, restarts, per namespace) — use it for 'how many / which are unhealthy / what restarts most' instead of reading rows. view='names' returns just names. view='table' (default) returns rows. Filter at the source: fieldSelector (status.phase!=Running, spec.nodeName=x) and labelSelector. Namespace auto-scoped unless allNamespaces=true.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "allNamespaces": {
            "description": "List across all namespaces (-A); ignored when the user selected a namespace",
            "type": "boolean",
          },
          "fieldSelector": {
            "description": "Field selector, e.g. status.phase=Failed",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "labelSelector": {
            "description": "Label selector, e.g. app=api or 'app in (a,b)'",
            "maxLength": 200,
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!() ]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "name": {
            "description": "Optional specific name filter",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "resource": {
            "description": "Resource type: pods, deployments, services, nodes, jobs, events, …",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "view": {
            "description": "table (default) | summary (exact counts) | names",
            "enum": [
              "table",
              "summary",
              "names",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "wide": {
            "description": "Use -o wide (more columns); table view only",
            "type": "boolean",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "resource",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "k8s_list",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Describe a single resource (status, events summary, conditions). Prefer over huge -o yaml for diagnosis.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "description": "Resource name",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "namespace": {
            "description": "Namespace override if not the session default",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "resource": {
            "description": "Resource type, e.g. pod, deployment",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "resource",
          "name",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "k8s_describe",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Fetch recent logs from a pod (or deploy/NAME, svc/NAME). Use previous=true for the last crashed container.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "container": {
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "name": {
            "description": "Pod name or deploy/x / svc/x",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "namespace": {
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "previous": {
            "description": "Logs from previous crashed container",
            "type": "boolean",
          },
          "since": {
            "description": "Relative duration e.g. 15m, 1h",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "tail": {
            "description": "Lines to fetch (default 100)",
            "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
            "maximum": 500,
            "type": "integer",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "k8s_logs",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Free-form kubectl (WITHOUT the 'kubectl' prefix). Prefer k8s_list / k8s_describe / k8s_logs first. Context and namespace are auto-injected; -A is narrowed to the selected namespace. Deletes/drains are blocked. Mutating commands require human approval.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "command": {
            "description": "The kubectl command to run (without the 'kubectl' prefix)",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "command",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "kubectl",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "kubectl piped into text filters, for answers no other tool gives directly: counts by a field, grouping, searching output (e.g. kubectl get pods --no-headers | awk '{print $3}' | sort | uniq -c). Only kubectl plus filters reading stdin (jq, grep, awk, sed, sort, head, tail, wc, cut, uniq, tr, column); no files. Context/namespace auto-injected. Mutating kubectl inside bash requires human approval.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "command": {
            "description": "The shell command to execute",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "command",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "bash",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Continuously tail new log lines from a pod. Returns only lines emitted since the previous call (per session). Use this for watching, reproducing intermittent issues, or end-to-end debugging where you need fresh data. Optional 'grep' filters lines to those matching a pattern (case-insensitive). Optional 'sinceSeconds' (default 60) is only used on the very first call.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "container": {
            "description": "Container name (for multi-container pods)",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "grep": {
            "description": "Case-insensitive substring/regex to filter lines",
            "maxLength": 200,
            "type": "string",
          },
          "namespace": {
            "description": "Namespace",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "pod": {
            "description": "Pod name (or 'deploy/<name>' / 'svc/<name>')",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-\\/:,=!@]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "sinceSeconds": {
            "description": "Initial lookback window in seconds (default 60)",
            "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
            "maximum": 86400,
            "type": "integer",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "pod",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "monitor_logs",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Ask the human user a clarifying question and PAUSE the agent until they reply. Use ONLY when you genuinely need information you cannot infer (e.g. 'which pod is the entrypoint?', 'what request id should I trace?', 'should I include the staging namespace too?'). Prefer up to 4 short options when possible. Do NOT use this for confirmations of obvious actions.",
      "executes": false,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "options": {
            "description": "Optional short answer choices",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "maxItems": 6,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "question": {
            "description": "The question to ask the user (one sentence)",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "question",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "ask_human",
      "scoped": false,
    },
    {
      "description": "Render a visual dashboard card in the chat: KPI metrics, charts (bar/line/area/pie), ranked issues, and optional tables. REQUIRED for deployment/cluster health and dashboard requests after 1–2 kubectl gathers. Use real numbers only. Then stop calling tools and give a short summary.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "charts": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "data": {
                  "description": "Array of row objects, e.g. [{name:'api', restarts:12}]",
                  "items": {
                    "additionalProperties": {
                      "type": [
                        "string",
                        "number",
                        "null",
                      ],
                    },
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 40,
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "series": {
                  "items": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "key": {
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "label": {
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "key",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 6,
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "title": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "type": {
                  "enum": [
                    "bar",
                    "line",
                    "area",
                    "pie",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "xKey": {
                  "description": "Category/time key for cartesian charts; default 'name'",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "type",
                "series",
                "data",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 4,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "issues": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "detail": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "resource": {
                  "description": "e.g. pod/foo or deploy/bar",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "severity": {
                  "enum": [
                    "critical",
                    "warning",
                    "info",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "title": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "severity",
                "title",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 20,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "metrics": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "label": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "tone": {
                  "enum": [
                    "good",
                    "warn",
                    "bad",
                    "neutral",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "unit": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "value": {
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "number",
                  ],
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "label",
                "value",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 12,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "score": {
            "description": "Optional health score 0–100",
            "maximum": 100,
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": "number",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "1–2 sentence executive read",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "tables": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "columns": {
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 8,
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "rows": {
                  "items": {
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "type": "array",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 40,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "title": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "columns",
                "rows",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 3,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Short board title, e.g. 'Namespace health'",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "title",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "present_dashboard",
      "scoped": false,
    },
    {
      "description": "Request rate, error rate and p50/p95 latency from traces (Tempo), grouped by service (default), endpoint (span name), version (ReplicaSet: compares a rollout's new pods with the old) or pod. Optionally for one workload. Start here for 'what is slow / failing / did the rollout make it worse', then traces_search for examples.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "groupBy": {
            "description": "service | endpoint | version | pod; default service",
            "enum": [
              "service",
              "endpoint",
              "version",
              "pod",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "namespace": {
            "description": "Namespace; default the one selected in the header",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "since": {
            "description": "Window, default 1h; Tempo measures at most 3h",
            "enum": [
              "15m",
              "1h",
              "6h",
              "24h",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "workloadKind": {
            "enum": [
              "deployment",
              "statefulset",
              "daemonset",
              "replicaset",
              "job",
              "cronjob",
              "pod",
              "service",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "workloadName": {
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "traces_stats",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Search log history in Loki: a namespace, a workload (all its pods, including pods that no longer exist) or one pod, over up to 7 days. Use it for pods that crashed or were replaced, errors kubectl's tail no longer has, or lines around a trace's time. errorsOnly keeps error/exception/traceback lines.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "around": {
            "description": "ISO time (e.g. a trace's start): search ±2 minutes around it instead of \`since\`",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "contains": {
            "description": "Case-insensitive text a line must contain",
            "maxLength": 200,
            "type": "string",
          },
          "errorsOnly": {
            "type": "boolean",
          },
          "limit": {
            "description": "Default 80 (the newest)",
            "maximum": 200,
            "minimum": 1,
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "namespace": {
            "description": "Namespace; default the one selected in the header",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "pod": {
            "description": "One pod (may no longer exist)",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "since": {
            "description": "Default 1h",
            "enum": [
              "15m",
              "1h",
              "6h",
              "24h",
              "7d",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "workloadKind": {
            "enum": [
              "deployment",
              "statefulset",
              "daemonset",
              "replicaset",
              "job",
              "cronjob",
              "pod",
              "service",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "workloadName": {
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "logs_search",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Find traces (Tempo) in the selected cluster: by workload or service, failing ones (errorsOnly), slow ones (minDuration), or any TraceQL condition (where, e.g. span.http.route = "/login" or span.http.response.status_code >= 500). Matches requests and consumed messages unless allSpans. Returns trace ids; read one with trace_get.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "allSpans": {
            "description": "Match every span, not only requests and consumed messages",
            "type": "boolean",
          },
          "errorsOnly": {
            "type": "boolean",
          },
          "limit": {
            "description": "Default 15",
            "maximum": 20,
            "minimum": 1,
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "minDuration": {
            "description": "e.g. 500ms, 2s",
            "pattern": "^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?(ms|s|m)$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "namespace": {
            "description": "Namespace; default the one selected in the header",
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "since": {
            "description": "Window, default 1h",
            "enum": [
              "15m",
              "1h",
              "6h",
              "24h",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "where": {
            "description": "Extra TraceQL condition on span./resource. attributes; no braces or pipes",
            "maxLength": 300,
            "type": "string",
          },
          "workloadKind": {
            "description": "deployment, statefulset, daemonset, pod, service, …",
            "enum": [
              "deployment",
              "statefulset",
              "daemonset",
              "replicaset",
              "job",
              "cronjob",
              "pod",
              "service",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "workloadName": {
            "pattern": "^[\\w.\\-]+$",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "traces_search",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Read one trace (Tempo) by id: services involved, errors with exception messages, the slowest spans and the call tree.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "traceId": {
            "description": "Trace id from traces_search or the user",
            "pattern": "^[0-9a-fA-F]{16,32}$",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "traceId",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "trace_get",
      "scoped": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Call one read-only tool on the team's Grafana (MCP). Pass {tool, arguments}. Use it for Loki logs, Prometheus metrics, dashboards, alert rules and incidents; most query tools need a datasourceUid: get it from list_datasources first.
Tools (* = required):
- list_datasources(type: string): List the data sources.
- query_prometheus(datasourceUid*: string, expr*: string): Run a PromQL query.",
      "executes": true,
      "input": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "arguments": {
            "additionalProperties": {},
            "description": "The tool's arguments as an object",
            "type": "object",
          },
          "tool": {
            "description": "Grafana MCP tool name from the list",
            "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,63}$",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "tool",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "grafana",
      "scoped": true,
    },
  ],
}
`;

